==Battleground==
*3 [[Capy|Capies]] spawn after 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[J.K. Bun Bun]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Berserkory]] spawns.
**Infinite [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn, delay 13.33~23.33 seconds<sup>400f~700f</sup>.
**1 [[Capy]] spawns.
**3 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**2 [[Pigge]]s spawn, delay 16.67~30 seconds<sup>500f~900f</sup>.
**13 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
**1 [[Professor A.]] spawns.

==Strategy==
The most important parts of this stage is to stall the 3 Capies at the beginning, and to kill the Berserkory. Cats like [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] can be helpful for stalling at the start, as money is very tight in this stage. Try to eliminate 2 of the Capies and save the last one for money stalling. The boss shockwave is also a problem. There is a Professor A, but a combination of [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe]] and [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier]] should work well. Courier also works wonders on the other red threats in the stage.

The most threatening part of this stage is the Berserkory, as he can cripple your meatshields, which lets the J.K. Bun Bun or the Capies kill your attackers. [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]], [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]], and [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Dread Pirate Catley]] all help in preventing this from happening. Talented Dread Pirate Catley is even better, as the Berserkory's waves will not affect him. Synergy with [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier]] will demolish Berserkory. Good Ubers for this stage include [[Thundia (Uber Rare Cat)|Thundia]], [[EVA Unit-02 (Uber Rare Cat)|EVA Unit-02]], [[Mighty Drednot (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Drednot]], [[Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Machine]], or any other anti-Red attackers or debuffers.

